Subject: [PATCH 02120/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE D1
 (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING -- the mandated self-learning experiment; fix the
 .396 bug) -- re-run online verifier-weight adaptation with the Tier-2 arm
 FIXED + a retrieval-augmented arm. research-program.md mandates >=1
 self-learning experiment/milestone (Tier-1 = online counter updates, CPU,
 <1us/update). .396 (exp4283) reported powered static-is-the-ceiling BUT was
 FLAGGED TAUTOLOGY because the Tier-2 arm was a NO-OP
 (tier2_cross_family_delta == static_cross_family_delta == 0.5 exactly) -- so
 the powered null is SUSPECT (the tier-2 mechanism did nothing). FIX the
 Tier-2 constraint-memory arm so it is a genuinely distinct mechanism (cache
 per-generator selection patterns, reuse on the nearest-neighbor seen
 generator), AND add a Tier-2 RETRIEVAL-augmented selector-context arm
 (Decocted 2604.04373: retrieval-only context on held-out families, NO weight
 mutation, NO LoRA). Re-run across the combined family set (the .395 manifest
 + exp4291's non-degenerate ARC-GEN generators, a soft input). Report static
 vs online vs tier2-memory vs tier2-retrieval cross-family delta + a POWERED
 CI95 on (best-adaptive - static). Emit online_adaptation_helps BARE bool :=
 (best-adaptive - static > 0 AND CI95-excl-0). verifier_is_oracle=false. NO
 fine-tuning; NO TRM; NO live-LoRA. A null WITH a working tier-2 = static is
 genuinely the ceiling (retire the ask).

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
